      "writtenOn": "2026-10-26T11:44:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Pim, much appreciated. PS3 addresses all five comments. Answers inline; summary of testing:\n\n- ixgbe (82599, lab + production DBN/CPT): DDM optics (SFF-8472). Before the change, a `show interface transceiver` of 2 ports took 1.47 s with the box stalled (20.3 % loss at 100 pps through VPP, main-thread probe max 1481 ms). After: 0 % loss, probe max 3 ms; a diag read still takes ~0.79 s, but only for the vppctl that asked. Cached repeats 0.00 s.\n- ixgbe, passive DAC (SFPP-PC015, SFF-8472 without DDM, on DBN): served as SFF-8079 (A0h only), module info works, diag says not available; no A2h NACK storm.\n- i40e (X710, core01): ~0.28 s per module through the AdminQ; same behaviour, no stalls.\n- Empty cage: not measured yet. All the boxes I have are remote and fully populated, so I can\u0027t pull a module. From the ixgbe code path I expect get_module_info to fail after its I2C retries (about 1 s, the same as a NACKed byte on a DAC, which I did see). That error is then cached: for 2 s in PS2, 30 s in PS3. I\u0027ll add a measurement once I can test an empty cage on site.\n- Not tested: ice, mlx5, bnxt or other PMDs; I don\u0027t have that hardware. As you found, they all honour info-\u003eoffset, and nothing here is PMD-specific beyond that. If you or anyone at IPng could run `show interface transceiver` on ice/mlx5 with this change, that would be great.\n- There is no `make test` coverage: the test framework has no transceiver to read, and the dpdk plugin isn\u0027t exercised by make test. The lab script I used (a 100 pps ping through VPP plus a 50 ms main-thread probe during reads, an admin down/up mid-read, and DOM value comparison) is available if useful.\n\nOn stale/missing/broken optics making other optics stale on a large box: there is one reader thread, so reads are serialised, round-robin across ports. Every PMD call returns (good or error); nothing loops in the reader. A broken or empty port costs one failed read (roughly 1 s on ixgbe, where get_module_info itself NACKs), and with PS3 that happens at most every 30 s and only when someone asks (CLI). There is no background polling in this change. A waiting CLI times out after 15 s of its own read (120 s including queueing), so a bad port can delay a read of another port by at most one failed read, and never forwarding or the main loop.\n\nFollow-up: https://gerrit.fd.io/r/c/vpp/+/47237 makes `show hardware-interfaces` mp-safe as well. With 47213 in, it was the last command that still paused forwarding around module info (19 ms per run on DBN; 3.1 ms on the lab with the change, the same as idle). It\u0027s small; would you mind having a look at it too?",
      "parentUuid": "42f1bddf_0db54f09",
      "revId": "c437742035940c69287b86f867521fab99e74427",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
