      "writtenOn": "2026-10-26T11:44:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confirmed: every rte_eth_dev_get_module_info / get_module_eeprom call is synchronous and returns. An empty cage or a module without I2C makes get_module_info fail after the PMD\u0027s own I2C retries (on ixgbe roughly 1 s; I haven\u0027t been able to measure an empty cage yet, as my boxes are remote and fully populated). The reader records last_rv, bumps the generation and goes idle, so nothing is retried in a loop. Callers get \"EEPROM read error for interface X (rv)\", and `show hardware detail` shows \"unknown\". With PS3 that error is cached for 30 s (see the next comment), and a port start/stop invalidates it, so a newly inserted module is read right after an admin down/up, and otherwise within 30 s.",
      "parentUuid": "cbecdfb4_e864fae9",
      "revId": "c437742035940c69287b86f867521fab99e74427",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
